{% set local_problem %}
<p>Madison sits on clay soil that doesn't absorb water well. Many neighborhoods also have high water tables, especially those closer to the Tennessee River watershed. When you combine that with 55+ inches of annual rainfall, simple downspout extensions just don't cut it.</p>

<p>Surface extensions move water a few feet from your foundation — then it just sits on the clay, finds the path of least resistance, and often ends up right back against your home. Underground drains solve this by routing water far enough away that it can't return.</p>

<p>For Madison homes with persistent water problems — wet basements, foundation cracks, eroded landscaping, standing water after storms — underground drains are often the only permanent solution. They're an investment, but far less expensive than foundation repairs.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Underground drains are buried pipes that connect to your downspouts and carry water away from your home through a sealed, sloped channel. The water exits at a predetermined point far from your foundation — typically at the property edge, a storm drain, or a dry well.</p>

<p>We use 4-inch corrugated or PVC pipe, depending on the application. The system is designed with proper slope (typically 1-2% grade) to ensure water flows away rather than pooling in the pipe. Pop-up emitters or daylight exits release the water at the discharge point.</p>

<p>Unlike French drains (which collect groundwater), underground gutter drains specifically handle roof runoff. They work in conjunction with your gutter system to create complete water management — from roof to safely away from your home.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've installed underground drainage systems throughout Madison County for over 20 years. We understand the soil conditions, water table challenges, and drainage patterns specific to this area.</p>

<p>Our systems are designed to last decades with minimal maintenance. We use quality materials, proper installation techniques, and thoughtful design to ensure your drainage problem is solved permanently — not just patched.</p>
{% endset %}
